Sounds good. But just so you know, if some network configuration causes websockets to fail, the SockJS library we use will fall back to more traditional connection methods, which will probably exhibit the slowness you were seeing. If you care about that, I'd play with your Apache mod_proxy buffer size, probably a small buffer size will help here; or perhaps easier to add this configuration directive to Shiny Server: "disable_protocols xdr-streaming xhr-streaming;"

